{"id": "EUVD-2026-82140", "enisaUuid": "37b01a45-0973-3e67-87ad-8dc469c8c194", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv, bpf: Fix memory leak in bpf_jit_free\n\nWhen bpf_int_jit_compile() is called for subprograms, it returns early\nduring the first pass (!prog->is_func || extra_pass is false), keeping\nctx->offset alive for the subsequent extra pass.\n\nIf JIT compilation fails for a later subprogram, the BPF core aborts\nand calls bpf_jit_free() to clean up the first subprogram. However,\nbpf_jit_free() fails to free jit_data->ctx.offset, which causes a\nmemory leak of the JIT context offsets array.\n\nFix this by adding the missing kfree(jit_data->ctx.offset) in\nbpf_jit_free().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7285f004293e7dc043c55369c0dbe8350b28cc45", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b594c23f584ab032a5eae809eee81b809dd27330", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cadc66b534fe8140441916200a20c7efb06a388", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a3a29e90021806ea00527f6458cfd2edb58b42a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/369e4635d04801f394d5bd42556f21029e95ff93"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-92519", "GHSA-94hw-5j8j-hwq4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1aa5b2bd-ced8-3d9e-a7a3-9f0569ce9811", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "1d93d927-ba44-381d-8956-bb277355c90b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2843fde6-c3a8-3dba-a64a-1dd1c811fd2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "28594b7a-8557-3252-877c-192e398c14df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48a8f78c50bd6f7f08fd40daa62252fd043f2f18 <5cadc66b534fe8140441916200a20c7efb06a388"}, {"id": "30060543-8af2-36e2-9da6-2b6925c6a6cc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8b21d00c-9cad-3d39-8916-3fc31f90e106", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48a8f78c50bd6f7f08fd40daa62252fd043f2f18 <b594c23f584ab032a5eae809eee81b809dd27330"}, {"id": "a9461f0c-70b9-3306-a8fc-c5f65ce511b9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ad65fa9a-f92b-39ed-9208-5886c77d915f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "c76cc044-eb65-3649-b5ca-9e76e1b83395", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48a8f78c50bd6f7f08fd40daa62252fd043f2f18 <7285f004293e7dc043c55369c0dbe8350b28cc45"}, {"id": "d0caaa3b-d6bc-38e7-bc4c-e0d3ee20b853", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "f4c954b3-0fda-32b4-844d-86b047a8e0e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48a8f78c50bd6f7f08fd40daa62252fd043f2f18 <2a3a29e90021806ea00527f6458cfd2edb58b42a"}, {"id": "fca6c22e-dbdf-39b1-baf2-d168b465f2b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48a8f78c50bd6f7f08fd40daa62252fd043f2f18 <369e4635d04801f394d5bd42556f21029e95ff93"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b9b211c4-615c-39d3-95b0-af622401c8e5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}